# What is and is not a source, for everything under reporting/.
#
# One file rather than one per document folder: a second document would other-
# wise need its own copy, and copies drift. Patterns here are matched against
# every path below reporting/, so a new folder inherits these rules without anyone
# remembering to set it up.
#
# THE RULE: git holds the things a person writes -- .tex, .py, .mmd, .md that
# was typed rather than generated, and the images/ that cannot be regenerated.
# Everything a script produces is excluded, however useful it is. A generated
# table or figure that is also committed is a second copy of the truth, and the
# committed one is the one that goes quietly stale while still looking official.
# The cost is that a fresh clone must run reporting/regenerate.sh once before the
# manual will compile. That is the intended trade.

# ---- generated ------------------------------------------------------------
# out/ holds everything any generator produces: the .md and .tex tables from
# stats/*.py, the .pdf figures, the workbook, and latexmk's own output under
# out/manual/. One directory, one line. Nothing in it is reviewable in a diff
# and all of it comes back from `./regenerate.sh`, so none of it is kept.
out/

# A .tex or .pdf that escaped out/ -- a stray run with an explicit --tex path,
# or a figure rendered in place. The .tex files that ARE sources live in
# diagrams/ and manual/, and are tracked already, so these patterns cannot
# reach them: .gitignore does not untrack a file git is already following.
*.aux
*.fdb_latexmk
*.fls
*.log
*.out
*.toc
*.xdv
*.synctex.gz
*.pdf
*.xlsx
*.csv

# Python leavings from running the generators.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# ---- not sources -----------------------------------------------------------
# Superseded originals -- the Word manual, the first timelines -- kept on disk
# for reference. Deliberately NOT in git: they are binaries that cannot be
# diffed or reviewed, they will never be edited again, and adding them would
# put them in the repo's history permanently.
archive/

# macOS
.DS_Store
